/// NodeVersionSkew — system event announced when a newly connected peer runs
/// a different wire-format or Beamtalk version (ADR 0126 §5.3, Amendment
/// (BT-5193) D3).
///
/// Published on `SystemAnnouncer current` by the runtime's
/// `beamtalk_node_monitor` once per connect, alongside `NodeShapeSkew`. A
/// peer that cannot report its versions (too old, or too slow to answer)
/// is announced too, with `nil` remote fields. The connection is never refused: a Beamtalk version
/// mismatch is the normal state of a rolling upgrade (ADR 0125). The
/// per-message wire-version check (`wire_version_unsupported`, ADR 0126
/// §5.2) stays the safety net.
///
/// ## Examples
/// ```beamtalk
/// SystemAnnouncer current when: NodeVersionSkew do: [:e |
///   Transcript showCr: e node name asString ++ " runs " ++ e remoteBeamtalkVersion printString
/// ]
/// ```
sealed typed Announcement subclass: NodeVersionSkew
  field: node :: Node
  field: localWireVersion :: Integer
  field: remoteWireVersion :: Integer | Nil = nil
  field: localBeamtalkVersion :: String
  field: remoteBeamtalkVersion :: String | Nil = nil
